      "content": "PART A: HUMAN WANTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Human wants are unlimited, whereas resources available to satisfy them are inherently scarce.",
        "Scarcity forces decision-makers to make choices, which inherently involves sacrifice.",
        "Opportunity cost represents the value of the next best alternative foregone.",
        "Production relies on four essential factors: Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship.",
        "The Production Possibility Curve (PPC) demonstrates maximum production limits under fixed technology and resources."
      ],
      "id": "sxanq9j"
